.TH WAYHUD 5 "2026-09-09" "wayhud" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
wayhud \- configuration file for wayhud(1)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/wayhud/config.toml
.PP
.RI ( ~/.config/wayhud/config.toml
when
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset, empty, or not an absolute path.)
.SH DESCRIPTION
The file is TOML. It holds one table,
.BR style ,
whose sub\-tables are named presets; a preset is chosen at run time with
.BR "wayhud \-\-style " \fINAME\fR
and defaults to
.BR default .
.PP
A missing file uses built-in defaults. Malformed files, unknown keys and
unknown preset names are errors.
.PP
.B [style.default]
is the base for every other preset. A key a preset does not set is taken from
there, then from the built\-in default listed below.
.PP
Sub\-tables
.RB ( reveal ,
.BR vanish ,
.BR sound )
merge key by key. A
.B kind
that differs from the base replaces the sub\-table, discarding fields from
the previous variant.
.PP
Command\-line flags override the selected preset for that invocation; see
.BR wayhud (1).
.SH VALUE TYPES
.TP
.I colour
Any colour GTK's CSS parser accepts:
.BR #b8bb26 ,
.BR #b8bb26cc ,
.BR "rgba(184,187,38,0.8)" ,
or a named colour such as
.BR green .
.TP
.I font
A Pango font description \- family, optional style words, then size in
points, e.g.\&
.B "\(dqMonospace 72\(dq"
or
.BR "\(dqFiraCode Nerd Font 72\(dq" .
Messages are plain text; Pango markup is not interpreted.
.IP
.BR Monospace ,
.B Sans
and
.B Serif
are fontconfig generics. Unavailable named families fall back to the system
font silently. Check a family with
.BR fc\-match (1).
.TP
.I pixels
Logical pixels, i.e.\& before the output's scale factor is applied. On a
.B scale 2
display a value of 64 covers 128 device pixels.
.SH KEYS
All keys below live directly in a
.BI [style. NAME ]
table.
.SS Text
.TP
.B font
.RI ( font ,
default
.BR "\(dqMonospace 72\(dq" )
.br
Typeface and size. The default uses the system's monospace font.
.TP
.B color
.RI ( colour ,
default
.BR \(dq#b8bb26\(dq )
.br
Fill colour of the glyphs.
.TP
.B outline
.RI ( colour ,
default
.BR \(dq#1d2021\(dq )
.br
Stroke colour. Set to
.B \(dqnone\(dq
to disable the outline, including one inherited from
.BR [style.default] .
.TP
.B outline_width
.RI ( float ,
.IR pixels ;
default: derived from the font size)
.br
Stroke width, from 0 to 128 logical pixels. Defaults to font size / 14.
.TP
.B glow
.RI ( table ,
default: absent)
.br
A soft halo behind the glyphs:
.BR "{ color = " \fICOLOUR\fR ", radius = " \fIF\fR ", alpha = " \fIF\fR " }" .
Absent by default; presets can inherit it from [style.default].
.RS
.TP
.B color
.RI ( colour ,
default
.BR \(dq#b8bb26\(dq )
The halo's colour.
.TP
.B radius
(float, 0\(en128
.IR pixels ;
default
.BR 12.0 )
Maximum halo reach in logical pixels. Set to
.B 0
to disable inherited glow. Increasing the radius adds padding and reduces
the available wrapping width.
.TP
.B alpha
(float, 0\(en1; default
.BR 0.55 )
Peak opacity of the halo where it leaves the glyph.
.RE
.IP
The halo is painted behind the outline.
.TP
.B scanlines
.RI ( table ,
default: absent)
.br
Dimmed horizontal bands cut through the message:
.BR "{ period = " \fIF\fR ", strength = " \fIF\fR ", duty = " \fIF\fR " }" .
Absent by default; a preset can inherit one from [style.default].
.RS
.TP
.B period
(float, 2\(en128
.IR "device pixels" ;
default
.BR 4.0 )
Distance between band centres. Unlike every other length here this is in
device pixels, not logical ones: the raster is a property of the screen, so it
keeps its pitch whatever the font size or the output scale.
.TP
.B strength
(float, 0\(en1; default
.BR 0.35 )
How far a band dims what is under it.
.B 0
is off \- which is how a preset takes back a raster inherited from
.BR [style.default] ,
TOML having no null, the same reason
.B outline
needs the literal
.BR \(dqnone\(dq .
.TP
.B duty
(float, 0 to below 1; default
.BR 0.5 )
Fraction of each period the band covers.
.B 1
would erase the message, so it is refused.
.RE
.IP
The bands are applied over the finished message, so they cut the halo as well
as the glyphs. They are painted inside the existing padding and, unlike
.BR glow.radius ,
do not widen it.
.TP
.B lines
.RI ( integer ,
default: the measured text)
.br
Height of the block in lines. Left unset, the surface is sized from the
message. Set, the room is reserved up front, so a message growing inside the
block does not resize the surface; the reserved room a message has not reached
is transparent and not visible.
.IP
This is also how much a listener keeps: see
.B LISTENER
in
.BR wayhud (1).
.TP
.B line_align
.RB ( left " | " center " | " right ,
default
.BR left )
.br
How lines are aligned relative to each other inside the text block. This is
independent of where the block itself sits.
.SS Placement
.TP
.B halign
.RB ( left " | " center " | " right ,
default
.BR center )
.br
Horizontal placement using physical edges, independent of text direction.
.TP
.B valign
.RB ( top " | " center " | " bottom ,
default
.BR center )
.br
Vertical placement.
.TP
.B margin
.RI ( integer ,
.IR pixels ;
default
.BR 64 )
.br
Gap from the anchored screen edge to the surface. Visible text is inset
further by padding for the outline, glow and caret. Padding grows with font
size and glow radius; caret width adds horizontal padding only.
.IP
Centred axes ignore this value.
.TP
.B width
.RI ( integer ,
.IR pixels ;
default: the measured text)
.br
Width of the text block, excluding the padding around it. Left unset, lines
wrap to the monitor and the surface is sized from the text that results, so a
short message gets a narrow surface and a long one a wide surface.
.IP
Set, it is both the wrapping budget and the width of the block, whatever the
message: text wraps at this value and the surface keeps this width. Since the
surface is transparent, room the message does not use is not visible, so
pinning it costs nothing to look at and stops the block resizing from one
message to the next.
.IP
A value wider than the monitor is clamped to it. Wider than the screen the
block would be clipped at both edges, and
.B line_align
would place lines outside the surface entirely.
.IP
This is also what makes
.B line_align
do something for a short message: with the block sized from the text there is
no room inside it to align within.
.SS Timing
.TP
.B timeout_ms
.RI ( integer ,
milliseconds; default
.BR 5000 )
.br
Hold time after reveal. The total reveal, hold and vanish duration must not
exceed 3600000 ms (one hour). Overlays cannot be dismissed early.
.TP
.B reveal
.RI ( table ,
default
.BR "{ kind = \(dqtypewriter\(dq, cps = 28, cursor = true }" )
.br
How the text appears. See
.B REVEAL
below.
.TP
.B vanish
.RI ( table ,
default
.BR "{ kind = \(dqcollapse\(dq, ms = 420 }" )
.br
How it goes away. See
.B VANISH
below.
.SS Sound
.TP
.B sound
.RI ( table ,
default
.BR "{ enabled = true, freq = 2100.0, decay_ms = 38.0, gain = 0.22, every = 1 }" )
.br
The typewriter blip. See
.B SOUND
below.
.SH THE COMMAND LINE
CLI flags override individual fields in the selected preset. For example:
.B \-\-glow \(aq#b8bb26,radius=12\(aq
sets glow colour and radius, preserving the preset's alpha.
.PP
CLI values use the same ranges as config values.
.B \-\-timeout
uses seconds;
.B timeout_ms
uses milliseconds. The CLI's
.B \-\-outline width=
sets
.BR outline_width .
See
.BR wayhud (1)
for all flags.
.SH REVEAL
A table with a
.B kind
key selecting the variant.
.TP
.B { kind = "instant" }
The whole message appears at once.
.TP
.BR "{ kind = \(dqtypewriter\(dq, cps = " \fIF\fR ", cursor = " \fIBOOL\fR ", jitter = " \fIF\fR ", scroll = " \fIBOOL\fR " }"
Typed out character by character.
.RS
.TP
.B cps
(float, default 28) Speed in characters per second. Must be positive; for no
typewriter the kind must say
.BR instant .
.TP
.B cursor
(boolean, default true) Draw a block caret at the write head. It keeps
blinking while the text is held.
.TP
.B jitter
(float, 0\(en1; default 0) Vary each keystroke interval by up to this fraction
in either direction. For example, 0.3 gives up to 30% variation. Audio and
animation use the same timings.
.TP
.B scroll
(boolean, default false) Keep the current line at the bottom of the block
and scroll earlier lines up. When false, fill from the top.
.IP
The surface remains fixed at the full message size in both modes. This works
at any position; single-line messages render identically. During
.BR untype ,
the scroll reverses as lines are erased.
.RE
.SH VANISH
A table with a
.B kind
key. Every variant except
.B instant
and
.B untype
takes
.B ms
(integer, default 420) for its duration.
.PP
.B untype
takes
.B cps
(float, default 60) instead, because it is the one effect that works a
character at a time. A fixed duration would erase a long message faster per
character than a short one, and a listener's block, which grows as messages
arrive, would vanish quicker the more it held. Timing it as a rate makes three
lines take three times as long as one, and matches
.B reveal.cps
so that typing in and erasing out are stated in the same unit.
.TP
.B instant
Gone on the frame the hold expires.
.TP
.B fade
Alpha to zero.
.TP
.B collapse
CRT power\-off: the text squashes towards its middle line, blooms slightly
wider, washes to white and blinks out.
.TP
.B wash
A soft edge sweeps through the text, erasing as it passes. Takes an extra
.B dir
of
.B down
(default) or
.BR up .
.TP
.B untype
Erase characters in reverse order with sound and a caret, including after
an instant reveal. Takes
.B cps
rather than
.BR ms .
.TP
.B dissolve
Disappear in blocks with fixed pseudo\-random lifetimes.
.SH SOUND
Blips are synthesised at run time. Parameter names match
.BR blyamk (1);
values from
.B blyamk \-v
can be copied into this table.
.TP
.B enabled
(boolean, default
.BR true )
.br
Enable blips.
.B \-\-sound off
overrides this to false, and
.B \-\-sound on
back to true, preserving the other parameters.
.TP
.B freq
(float, 100\(en8000 Hz; default
.BR 2100.0 )
.br
Base frequency of the blip \- its overall pitch.
.TP
.B decay_ms
(float, 10\(en3000 milliseconds; default
.BR 38.0 )
.br
Decay time of the blip.
.TP
.B gain
(float, 0\(en1; default
.BR 0.22 )
.br
Peak amplitude of a single blip. Overlapping blips sum and are clamped to
full scale. High gain at high
.B cps
will clip.
.TP
.B every
(integer, at least 1; default
.BR 1 )
.br
Blip once every N revealed characters. Whitespace is silent.
.SH EXAMPLE
Only
.B [style.default]
spells out the common settings; the others state their differences.
.PP
More presets and optional settings are shipped in
.I config.example.toml
in the source distribution.
.PP
.RS
.nf
[style.default]
font = "FiraCode Nerd Font 72"   # check with fc-match
color = "#b8bb26"
outline = "#1d2021"
halign = "center"
valign = "center"
timeout_ms = 5000
reveal = { kind = "typewriter", cps = 28, cursor = true }
vanish = { kind = "collapse", ms = 420 }

# Inherits font, outline and placement from default.
[style.alert]
color = "#fb4934"
timeout_ms = 8000
vanish = { kind = "wash", ms = 300, dir = "up" }

# Typewriter reveal and reverse erase.
[style.spy]
color = "#8ec07c"
reveal = { kind = "typewriter", cps = 18, cursor = true }
vanish = { kind = "untype", cps = 20 }

# Scroll from the bottom-left corner.
[style.boot]
font = "Monospace 28"
halign = "left"
valign = "bottom"
margin = 32
reveal = { kind = "typewriter", cps = 40, cursor = true, scroll = true }
vanish = { kind = "fade", ms = 300 }

# Small, silent corner overlay.
[style.corner]
font = "Monospace 24"
halign = "right"
valign = "bottom"
margin = 32
reveal = { kind = "instant" }
vanish = { kind = "fade", ms = 200 }
sound = { enabled = false }
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wayhud (1)
